Rackett is an independent, experimental rewrite inspired by Jackett.
It is not an official Jackett release and is not affiliated with its maintainers.

Upstream research baseline:
https://github.com/Jackett/Jackett
commit fe8876d21b93dfda84eb12bd24e1c72e56fb8736

Jackett upstream source and documentation are distributed under GNU GPL version 2.
This repository is distributed under GPL-2.0-only; see LICENSE.
Rackett's Rust code is a new implementation. Its Cardigann behaviour was
reimplemented by studying Jackett's GPL-2.0 source at the commit above, so
Rackett is distributed under the same license family and credits the Jackett
contributors, including the community authors of every tracker definition.
The pinned upstream tracker definition catalog, schema and model fixtures are
vendored under vendor/jackett with provenance, checksums and the upstream license.
No bundled upstream frontend library is shipped here.
Synthetic adapter fixtures are included for offline tests.

Rust dependencies retain their own licenses. Cargo.lock records exact versions;
tools/dependency_licenses.py produces a license inventory for the locked build.
